## Key Design Points

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Buffer over-read (uint64)** | Single check: `cursor + 8 > buf_len` before touching any bytes |
| **Buffer over-read (varint)** | Checked on every loop iteration *before* accessing `buf[cursor]` |
| **Malformed varint (infinite)** | Hard cap of 10 iterations — the theoretical maximum for a 64-bit value |
| **Cursor advancement** | Only moved forward on the success path; left unchanged on failure so the caller can try a different parse strategy |
| **Shift overflow** | `shift` reaches at most 63 (7 × 9), which is safe for a 64-bit type |

