## Two Different Types of Swaps

### 1. Swapping int* Contents (Values Pointed To)
This swaps the actual integers that two pointers point to.

### 2. Swapping int** Pointers (The Pointers Themselves)
This swaps which memory addresses two pointers point to.

The key difference: One swaps **what the pointers point to**, the other swaps **the pointers themselves**.

